.TH WAYLAND-SHARE-BRIDGE 1 "2026-10-20" "wayland-share-bridge 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayland-share-bridge \- share Wayland screens and windows with X11 applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wayland-share-bridge
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.B \-\-list-sources
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.RB [ \-\-reselect [= KIND ]]
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.B \-\-status
.br
.B wayland-share-bridge
.B \-\-quit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayland-share-bridge
captures a Wayland screen or window and paints every frame into an ordinary
X11 window.  X11 and XWayland applications (WPS Office, Zoom, Feishu, Electron
applications, browsers, OBS, ...) can capture that window like any other, even
though they cannot see native Wayland windows at all.
.PP
By default the bridge talks to the compositor directly through
.BR ext-image-copy-capture-v1 ;
screens are enumerated with
.BR wl_output
and windows with
.BR ext-foreign-toplevel-list-v1 .
The sources are offered in the tray menu, so switching between them is a
single click and no desktop portal picker is involved.
With
.BR \-\-portal
(or when the compositor lacks those protocols) the bridge falls back to the
.BR org.freedesktop.portal.ScreenCast
portal and the compositor's own picker.
.PP
The bridge window is invisible (via
.BR _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY
or a compositor window rule) and click-through (empty XFixes input region).
The installed launcher
.B wayland-share-bridge-launch
adds the Hyprland rule that hides the window.
.PP
A single instance runs per session and offers a tray icon (StatusNotifierItem
with a D-BusMenu) plus a small control interface on the session bus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cursor= MODE
Cursor mode for the portal backend: \fBhidden\fR, \fBembedded\fR (default) or
\fBmetadata\fR.  Direct capture paints the cursor for monitor sources.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-source\-kind= KIND
Fallback source kind for the portal backend: \fBauto\fR (default, remembers the
last choice), \fBany\fR, \fBscreen\fR or \fBwindow\fR.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-source= SPEC
Capture SPEC immediately:
.BI screen: NAME
or
.BI window: APP_ID
or
.IB window: APP_ID | TITLE \fR.
Names are the ones printed by \fB\-\-list\-sources\fR.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list\-sources
Print the screens and windows that can be shared, one per line as
.I kind:id<TAB>label\fR, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-portal
Always use the desktop portal (system picker) instead of direct capture.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remember
Remember the last source (default).  The state is stored in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/state ;
the portal restore token (when returned) in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/restore_token .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-remember
Do not remember the source.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-show
Show the bridge window.  Intended for debugging; it stays click-through.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title= TEXT
Window title.  Defaults to
.IR "Wayland Share Bridge" .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-token\-file= PATH
Use a custom restore token file for the portal backend.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tray
Do not create the tray icon and the control interface.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-multiple
Allow more than one running instance.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH TRAY MENU
The tray icon offers a flat menu:
.TP
.B Stop sharing
Stop mirroring; the bridge keeps running.
.TP
.B Show/Hide shared window
Toggle the visibility of the mirror window on your own screen.
.TP
.B Screen: NAME (WxH)
One click mirrors that monitor; the active source carries a checkmark.
.TP
.B Window: APP \- TITLE
One click mirrors that native Wayland window; the active source carries a
checkmark.
.TP
.B Share via system portal...
Runs the portal picker (same as \fB\-\-reselect\fR).
.TP
.B Quit
Stops the bridge.
.PP
The menu is flat because tray hosts hydrate nested submenus inconsistently.
It is refreshed every time the menu is opened, and the SNI tooltip shows the
current sharing status.
.SH CONTROLLING A RUNNING INSTANCE
.TP
.BR \-\-reselect [= KIND ]
Ask the portal for a new source, optionally restricted to
\fBKIND\fR (\fBany\fR, \fBscreen\fR or \fBwindow\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print what the running instance is sharing.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the running instance.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Ask the running instance to pick a new source through the portal.
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Stop the bridge.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Compositor connection used for direct capture.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X server connection (XWayland) used for the mirror window.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the remembered source and the portal restore token.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_SHARE_BRIDGE_BINARY
Binary executed by the launcher (default:
.BR wayland-share-bridge ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/state
Remembered source (\fIsource=screen:NAME\fR or \fIsource=window:APP_ID|TITLE\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/wayland-share-bridge/restore_token
Portal restore token, when the portal returns one.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge-launch
Start the bridge from a desktop session and use the tray menu.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --list-sources
See what can be shared, then pass one of the names to \fB\-\-source\fR.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --source=screen:DP-2
Share the monitor called DP-2.
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --no-tray --source='window:firefox|DeepSeek'
Share one window, run headless (no tray).
.TP
.B wayland-share-bridge --portal --cursor=hidden
Use the portal picker with the cursor hidden.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-desktop-portal (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR hyprctl (1)
